  {
   "id": "dH7XeR0XBgAJ",
   "from": "Jeffrey Doser",
   "author": "0b274a0ee3490d75",
   "date": "2024-11-07T17:33:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: MSOM with multiple taxonomic groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Thiago, <div><br></div><div>Just to add onto this, there unfortunately is no way to share information only across sub-groups in multi-species models in spOccupancy (or spAbundance), so one option would be to fit three separate msPGOcc() models and then combine/compare results of those three groups after the fact. Or, you could fit one big msPGOcc() with all species. The pros and cons of these sorts of approaches is outlined nicely from this paper back in 2014:<a href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.976\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.976&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CP5LJ_Hnxnv8Yr5Pv_mxP\"> https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.976</a>. </div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Jeff<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, November 7, 2024 at 8:05:18 AM UTC-5 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bicu...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Thank you so much André.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Cheers, </div><br clear=\"all\"></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:14px;line-height:normal\"><b style=\"font-style:inherit;text-align:-webkit-auto;font-size:10pt\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thiago Bicudo</font></b></div></div></div></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El jue, 7 nov 2024 a las 6:12, André Luís Luza (&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">luza....@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p dir=\"ltr\">Hello,</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">I think a similar question (with answer) already circulated here:</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/0HWn7OemeRo/m/zB987_c-AQAJ?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer&amp;pli=1\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/0HWn7OemeRo/m/zB987_c-AQAJ?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter%26pli%3D1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Uf5FyU5Svy4HKgN72MqAc\">https://groups.google.com/g/hmecology/c/0HWn7OemeRo/m/zB987_c-AQAJ?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer&amp;pli=1</a></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Best, </p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">André <br>\r\n</p>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Em qua., 6 de nov. de 2024 22:27, Thiago Bicudo &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">bicu...@gmail.com</a>&gt; escreveu:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br clear=\"all\"></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:14px;line-height:normal\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Dear all,</div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\">I have a dataset of detections and non-detections of birds, mammals, and amphibians from passive acoustic monitoring. I will run a multi-species occupancy model on these groups<span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> (</span>simultaneously<span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">) </span>to examine the effects of certain landscape variables on occupancy at the community level and produce a species richness map using a Z matrix.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">That being said, </span>Is there a practical way to keep the parameters for all 3 taxon groups separated when using msPGOcc()?</div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Thanks, </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Thiago Bicudo</div><br></div></div><div style=\"line-height:normal\"><div style=\"text-align:-webkit-auto\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline\"><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12pt;font-style:inherit;font-weight:inherit;margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:10pt;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline;color:inherit\"></span></p><p style=\"margin:0px\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;vertical-align:baseline\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"color:inherit;font-size:10pt;font-style:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"><a href=\"https://scholar.google.com.br/citations?user=gf1uMbYAAAAJ&amp;hl=pt-PT&amp;oi=ao\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://scholar.google.com.br/citations?user%3Dgf1uMbYAAAAJ%26hl%3Dpt-PT%26oi%3Dao&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Mru2TOxRskyDIZ7s7nLHb\">Scholar</a>  <a href=\"http://lattes.cnpq.br/4376981722714698\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lattes.cnpq.br/4376981722714698&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UV6JO9Db9S2byBz1wM1DG\">Lattes</a>  </font><span style=\"text-align:-webkit-auto;font-size:13.3333px\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://bicudotks.wordpress.com/\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bicudotks.wordpress.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1zOprNOR2Apxt-0krsKtVf\">Website</a>    <a href=\"https://github.com/bicudotks\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bicudotks&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464220324000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1C3GcMwEbwJfGqJTIRMIhE\">GitHub</